The critical refinement is that the ball shouldn’t hit every bumper.

It should encounter the right concepts, sometimes make a surprising jump, preserve constraints, and stop when it has produced enough value.

That is the difference between associative brainstorming and controlled cognitive exploration.

And I need external memory for this to scale. I can retrieve and combine relevant context, but I cannot literally keep every repository file or past thought simultaneously active in my working context. The graph, retrieval system, and state record are what make your intended continuity practical.

